  "notes": "Official cause_code is TBD in FORM-366 FIELDS, so cause node marked provisional per rule 4. No block_13 rows provided. Narrative states 1B EDG and Unit 1 CA system were both already removed from service for maintenance and thus did not auto-start on the valid sequencer signals -- this is not a component failure but a pre-existing maintenance condition, modeled as part of the consequence description rather than a separate BACKED_UP_BY edge (no explicit statement that 1B train was 'operable' during the window -- in fact it was inoperable due to maintenance). 1A train equipment is mentioned only in Safety Analysis as maintaining core/spent fuel cooling under design-basis train redundancy, not as an explicit operable backup system with a stated system name/code, so no System node created for it. No manufacturer or previous-occurrence LER referenced (report explicitly states none in past 3 years with same causal factor)."
